WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.579 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  it's January and chances are you've made  some kind of resolution to get in shape  or be healthier I know I have now I'm  not a big fan of going to the gym or  running or getting off the couch unless  it's absolutely necessary but I am a fan  of the gamification of exercise while  games like arms just dance and one two  switch have elements of physicality to  them and even calorie counters in the  case of Just Dance fitness boxing is  Nintendo's first dedicated exa gaming  release on switch and I was keen to  check it out having spent money on  actual boxing gloves I have never used I  was wary of dropping more dollars on the  idea of boxing and at $50 fitness boxing  is a little steep Nintendo and developer  Imagineer have released a free demo  fitness boxing which gives you an idea  of what to expect but the full version  features a number of really nice touches  like plugging in your own stats  customized workouts and changing  trainers quite apart from letting you  play for more than three daily workouts  and ten free sessions which the trial  version is limited to at a basic level  you'll be holding a joy con in each fist  and executing various punches in time  with a handful of instrumental versions  of top 40 songs the most interesting  feature is a customizable daily workout  where you can elect what areas to work  on your fitness goals and how long to  make each session I got about halfway  through my first daily workout before  severely regretting selecting 35 minute  sessions but the game had promised me  that this particular mashup of jabs  uppercuts and hooks would burn two  hundred and thirty-odd calories so I  reluctantly powered through I'm not  entirely sure where this number comes  from but I was absolutely working up a  sweat during the session and my arms  were sore for days afterwards though we  can't exactly confirm if that's just  down to my complete lack of fitness  learning to properly wind up punches so  you can deliver them in strings that  perfectly timed hits is satisfying and  the encouragement and guidance you  receive from your personal digital  trainer helps a lot  all right that's good aside from that  the game has a couple of two-player  modes if you can get a mate to bring  their joy cones over and loads of  different moves that make up each of the  free workout and daily sessions so the  segments are noticeably different every  time and get more complex as you go that  said I did experience some  inconsistencies with the motion control  mechanics the joy cones are great at  picking up movement but they don't  necessarily seem to mind which movement  it wasn't immediately obvious if I was  indeed miss timing punches or if the  wrong movement was being detected as  sometimes my wind-up for a punch would  register as the execution meaning my  timing would register as off coupled  with a lack of explanations of technique  and form for each punch this led to some  frustrating detection issues it also  seemed easier to judge punch timing by  the visual aids on screen and the  instructors count instead of the music  which was a bit of a shame but  ultimately you're still getting a  workout whether the system registers it  or not now I'm not one of those high on  the endorphins of fitness kinds of  people so the only way I can get through  it is to distract myself from the  crappiness of painful exercise given the  easy listening pop tracks weren't  distracting me enough from the torturous  act of working out nor were they  particularly helpful for timing I opted  to change up my tactics you have the  option to turn down the volume of the  trainer sound effects for background  music so I switched off the music in  favor of the most enjoyable distracting  thing I can imagine  back-to-back segments of last week  tonight with John Oliver you have six  intimidatingly fit trainers to choose  from who all have limited programmed  voice lines so get ready to hear alright  that's good so many times it'll work its  way into your dreams despite the muddly  robotic voices of most of the trainer's  being reminded to breathe keep your form  lift your hands and told when to deal a  blow is really helpful I chose the  trainer with an Australian accent as she  sounded the most natural to me but you  can swap between them as you go alright  let's get down to it you can also unlock  in your clothing items for each trainer  as well as extra songs by completing  workouts which is a smart way of making  workouts feel worth it when you reach  the end personally I usually treat  - a post-workout beer but this is  probably healthier while it won't  explicitly train you on proper form and  technique fitness boxing will definitely  help you work up a sweat if you put the  time in  holding the joy concers natural and easy  and having a daily reason to come back  is clever piecemeal motivation as is the  option to pile on extra practice  sessions if you're feeling particularly  workout inclined I've been playing  fitness boxing for just over a week and  it feels like just the right amount of  balance of gamification reward and  workout without having to leave the  couch for too long while I'm still  holding out the switch fit this one is a  good buy if you're already into the idea  of boxer size and it's worth keeping an  eye out for a sale if you're interested  eyes games but put off by the current  price tag  [Music]

